      "x-notes": "Upstream (openai/CLIP `_transform`: torchvision Resize(224, BICUBIC) + CenterCrop(224) on a PIL image): resize the shortest side to 224 with Pillow BICUBIC (long side int(224 * long / short)), center-crop 224 x 224 (offsets round((side - 224) / 2)), /255. transformers 5's CLIPImageProcessor floors the crop offset and resizes with torch, so it can differ by a pixel of offset on odd margins. OpenAI CLIP normalization (mean 0.48145466/0.4578275/0.40821073, std 0.26862954/0.26130258/0.27577711) is in the graph: feed RGB on [0,1]. The graph input is float16; the host builds float32 and converts."
