    "x-notes": "CLIP BPE (NFC, whitespace collapsed, lowercase; `</w>` end-of-word): BOS 49406, at most 75 pieces, EOS 49407, right-padded with 49407 to 77, as transformers' CLIPTokenizer does with padding='max_length', truncation=True. Only <|startoftext|> and <|endoftext|> are added tokens: '!' is an ordinary piece here ('hello!' -> 3306, 256), unlike SD 2.x's tokenizer, where '!' is the pad token 0. The graph takes no attention mask (causal attention makes it redundant) and pools the first EOS, so any pad id works. Rows of a bucket beyond the texts are filled with [BOS, EOS, then pad] and their outputs discarded."
